{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01PzC2UVMRmXG48X3ABXF1Sb", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hands_Across_Hawthorne\"}, {\"url\": \"https://newsandletters.org/july-august-2011-queer-notes/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/vm40xr72z/supplemental_files/1497\"}, {\"url\": \"https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/gx41mj13c/supplemental_files/3612\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/maybe-hold-hands-091600347.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/h128nf02d/supplemental_files/3564\"}, {\"url\": \"https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/q811kk06m/supplemental_files/4405\"}, {\"url\": \"https://betsyrobinson.substack.com/p/becoming-the-music\"}, {\"url\": \"https://washingtonian.com/?p=229464\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:23:22.773Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "\"Hands Across Hawthorne\" Forkner \"Queer Patrol\" crowd sang", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01NZJxRdjGVdoNf1hQFSxkpG", "content": [{"title": "Hands Across Hawthorne", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hands_Across_Hawthorne"}, {"title": "July-August 2011 Queer Notes", "url": "https://newsandletters.org/july-august-2011-queer-notes/"}, {"title": "av.lib.uh.edu", "url": "https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/vm40xr72z/supplemental_files/1497"}, {"title": "av.lib.uh.edu", "url": "https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/gx41mj13c/supplemental_files/3612"}, {"title": "Maybe we need to hold hands", "url": "https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/maybe-hold-hands-091600347.html"}, {"title": "av.lib.uh.edu", "url": "https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/h128nf02d/supplemental_files/3564"}, {"title": "av.lib.uh.edu", "url": "https://av.lib.uh.edu/media_objects/q811kk06m/supplemental_files/4405"}, {"title": "Becoming the Music", "url": "https://betsyrobinson.substack.com/p/becoming-the-music"}, {"title": "News & Politics", "url": "https://washingtonian.com/?p=229464"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything saying the crowd at Hands Across Hawthorne sang, and nothing linking a \"Queer Patrol\" to that rally.\n\nWhat the results do cover:\n\n- **The rally:** Hands Across Hawthorne was a rally held at the Hawthorne Bridge in Portland, Oregon, on May 29, 2011. It followed a attack, one week earlier, on Brad Forkner and Christopher Rosevear, a gay male couple who had been holding hands while walking across the bridge.\n- **Attendance and purpose:** Wikipedia reports that more than 4,000 people attended the rally, and that organizers aimed to link hands across the whole span of the bridge as a show of solidarity (Several LGBTQ and human rights organizations sponsored Hands Across Hawthorne in response to the attack).\n- **Queer Patrol:** Wikipedia says the attack prompted volunteers from the Q Center, a nonprofit organization that supports the LGBTQ community, to form street patrols. That connects the patrols to the same events, but the results don't describe them at the rally.\n- **Crowd behavior:** A 2011 newsletter describes over 4,000 protesters stood on Hawthorne Bridge in support of the couple, but it doesn't mention singing.\n\nThe other \"Queer Patrol\" hits are Houston radio transcripts about a different group and city, and a Yahoo piece about a \"Hands Across Owensboro\" event, so they don't apply. If you need to know whether there was singing, a 2011 Portland news report or the Q Center's own records would be the best next place to check."], "durationSeconds": 6.040650125, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01PzC2UVMRmXG48X3ABXF1Sb", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
